WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.045 --> 00:00:05.024
Ally was terrified. Melanie was racing straight toward her!

2
00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:07.672
"I'm doomed!" Ally thought.

3
00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:14.135
"Jorgandians can move fast. If I try to run, Melanie will instantly catch me."

4
00:00:14.136 --> 00:00:17.639
She took a deep breath and tried to calm herself.

5
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:21.366
"What would my parents tell me to do in this situation?"

6
00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:28.601
She remembered her father always saying, "Use your abilities, including your Astral mind."

7
00:00:28.602 --> 00:00:33.461
And her mother often said, "You're an Astralian, Allyzooba.

8
00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:38.147
We are brave, strong, and peaceful."

9
00:00:38.148 --> 00:00:44.759
"That's it!" Ally focused and read Melanie's mind: "There she is! I must catch her!"

10
00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.599
"Ack!" Ally thought.

11
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:53.127
"Melanie is trying to catch me!" Ally looked around, but there were no other humans in sight.

12
00:00:53.128 --> 00:00:55.903
"I know! I'll try to distract her."

13
00:00:55.904 --> 00:01:00.346
Ally tried to throw her voice, to make Melanie think someone was behind her.

14
00:01:00.347 --> 00:01:04.919
But she was so nervous, all that came out was a weak croak.

15
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.345
Melanie reached Ally.

16
00:01:07.346 --> 00:01:13.103
"Today's my lucky day! I found you alone!" she shouted in triumph.

17
00:01:13.104 --> 00:01:19.559
Ally shivered. "Fine." She threw up her hands, surrendering.

18
00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:26.114
"You've got me. Just please, if you're going to evaporate me, do it fast."

19
00:01:26.115 --> 00:01:34.569
"Oh, Ally, you're so funny!" Melanie laughed, then quickly turned serious.

20
00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:39.539
She looked around as if she was checking to make sure there were no humans nearby.

21
00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.539
"I'm going to give it to you straight, Ally."

22
00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.339
Ally drew in a breath.

23
00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:49.797
"Just do it fast, Melanie!" Ally pleaded.

24
00:01:49.798 --> 00:01:56.117
"Fine." Melanie whispered in Ally's ear. "It's me."

25
00:01:56.118 --> 00:02:01.383
"I know." Ally was trying to stay brave, but her voice wobbled.

26
00:02:01.384 --> 00:02:03.499
"I figured it out."

27
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:07.379
"You did?" Melanie looked shocked.

28
00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.759
"Yes, after you made that green smoothie," Ally said.

29
00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.859
"It tasted exactly like a Galorpian astroshake."

30
00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.108
"You really are a funny person."

31
00:02:20.109 --> 00:02:26.087
But this time Melanie wasn't laughing at Ally; she was just staring intently at her.

32
00:02:26.088 --> 00:02:30.983
Ally wiped her brow. "So, what do we do now?

33
00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:34.845
Do you take me back with you or . . . ?"

34
00:02:34.846 --> 00:02:37.119
Melanie looked confused.

35
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:42.268
"We, um, keep the secret between us for now. Can you do that?"

36
00:02:42.269 --> 00:02:46.606
"Whatever you want!" Ally said desperately. "Just don't—"

37
00:02:46.607 --> 00:02:49.554
"Great!" Melanie beamed.

38
00:02:49.555 --> 00:02:54.956
"I really don't want Ray to know I'm the one who recommended his diner to Big City Foods."

39
00:02:54.957 --> 00:02:58.119
Ally was stunned. "What?"

40
00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:02.270
"The CEO is an old friend of mine," Melanie continued.

41
00:03:02.271 --> 00:03:06.349
"He always asks me to recommend restaurants that I find on my travels.

42
00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:10.050
But it's better if I remain anonymous, just in case things don't work out.

43
00:03:10.051 --> 00:03:13.379
I wouldn't want Ray to wind up disappointed."

44
00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.434
Melanie looked at her watch.

45
00:03:15.435 --> 00:03:20.455
"I have to go. I'm meeting a friend for coffee. See you later!"

46
00:03:20.456 --> 00:03:27.519
She hurried off, calling back over her shoulder, "I'm glad you liked my smoothie!"

47
00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:31.298
Ally didn't know if she should laugh or faint.

48
00:03:31.299 --> 00:03:35.926
"Melanie's secret is about Ray's diner," she thought.

49
00:03:35.927 --> 00:03:42.939
"She's not the Jorgandian after all!" Ally wiped her brow again, this time in relief.

50
00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:51.430
But then she had a new scary thought. "If Melanie isn't the Jorgandian, who is?"

51
00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:56.439
Ally didn't get a chance to fill in Mateo until after they got home.

52
00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:02.899
"Guess what," Ally said. "Melanie is not the Jorgandian."

53
00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.119
"How do you know?" Mateo asked.

54
00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:11.619
"Because . . ." Ally was about to tell Mateo about the CEO of Big City Foods.

55
00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:16.119
Then she remembered that Ray wanted to tell Mateo that news himself.

56
00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:19.078
She pulled open the front door. "Well, you see—"

57
00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:24.562
"Mateo!" Ray called. "There you are.

58
00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:27.359
I need to speak to you about something important, son."

59
00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.611
"What's up, Papi?" Mateo said.

60
00:04:30.612 --> 00:04:34.639
"I'll leave you two alone," Ally said, heading to her room.

61
00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:39.082
"It's okay, Ally. Please stay." Ray stopped her.

62
00:04:39.083 --> 00:04:44.556
He looked nervous as he told Mateo about his call with the CEO of Big City Foods.

63
00:04:44.557 --> 00:04:49.379
Mateo frowned. "He wants you to sell the diner to him?"

64
00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:51.847
"Not exactly," Ray said.

65
00:04:51.848 --> 00:04:56.174
"He wants to expand the business into a whole chain of restaurants."

66
00:04:56.175 --> 00:04:59.792
"That doesn't mean they serve chains," Ally said.

67
00:04:59.793 --> 00:05:04.707
"I know what a restaurant chain is," Mateo said.

68
00:05:04.708 --> 00:05:07.706
"So, are you going to do it, Papi?"

69
00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:12.873
"I haven't decided yet. I want to hear what the CEO has to say in person."

70
00:05:12.874 --> 00:05:16.669
Mateo sighed, and Ally could tell he was upset.

71
00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:21.119
"You have to do what you think is best," Mateo said.

72
00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:27.238
"But the diner is our home, and I don't want you to change anything about it."

73
00:05:27.239 --> 00:05:40.265
"Me neither," Ally thought. "The diner is perfect, just like it is."

